\(\underset{$\text{ acetylene }}{\mathrm{HC}$ \equiv $\mathrm{CH}$}+\underset{$\text{ formaldehyde }}{\mathrm{HCHO}$}$\stackrel{\text{ High pressure }}{$\longrightarrow} $\mathrm{HC} \equiv \mathrm{C}-\mathrm{CH}_{2} \mathrm{OH}
\(\mathrm{HC} \equiv \mathrm{C}-\mathrm{CH}_{2} \mathrm{OH}+\mathrm{H}-\stackrel{\huge \mathrm{H} \atop |}{\mathrm{C}}=\mathrm{O} \longrightarrow \underset{\text{ But-2-yn, } 4 \text{ diol }}{\mathrm{HOCH}_2 \equiv \mathrm{CCH}_2 \mathrm{OH}}$
Therefore, acetylene with formaldehyde under high pressure forms by butyndiol.
